<title>HUNGARY: Budapest bourse P/E ratio rises to 16.49 in Dec.</title>
<headline>Budapest bourse P/E ratio rises to 16.49 in Dec.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The market price/earnings ratio rose to 16.49 in December from 14.79 in November, on the Budapest Stock Exchange (BSE), the BSE said in its monthly report.</p>
<p>The market price/book value rose to 1.63 from 1.46 in November.</p>
<p>The dividend yield dipped to 1.43 percent in December from 1.48 percent in November.</p>
<p>		    MARKET RATIOS ON THE BUDAPEST STOCK EXCHANGE</p>
<p>			  P/E ratio  P/BV ratio  Dividend yield(pct)</p>
<p>  Dec		    16.49	1.63	   1.43</p>
<p>  Nov		    14.79	1.46	   1.48</p>
<p>  Oct		    14.20	1.46	   1.53</p>
<p>  Sept		   13.89	1.43	   1.45</p>
<p>  Aug		    13.91	1.44	   1.45</p>
<p>  July		   13.89	1.28	   1.84</p>
<p>  June		   14.88	1.28	   1.88</p>
<p>  May		    14.03	1.19	   1.86 @</p>
<p>  April		  12.67	1.05	   1.86</p>
<p>  March		  12.09	1.01	   1.70</p>
<p>  February	     12.97	0.94	   1.50</p>
<p>  January		15.17	0.98	   1.50</p>
<p>  December 1995	10.90	0.70	   1.85</p>
<p>NOTE: The P/E ratios are calculated by dividing total share capitalisation by total after-tax results (profits and losses).</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
